cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this manuscript, these protocols, results or code, please cite this repository."
title: "PortabilityRisk: replicon-resolved, occurrence-level portability of acquired resistance genes in closed bacterial genomes"
abstract: >-
  Manuscript, frozen protocols, results, data resource, validation record and
  analysis code for a study of resistance-gene portability in 6,288 closed
  complete Gram-negative ESKAPE genomes. Each of 74,349 acquired
  resistance-gene occurrences is assigned to a documented chromosome or plasmid
  using NCBI molecule designations rather than prediction, and receives one of
  five evidence-ranked portability classes. The study reports that portability
  is a property of the occurrence rather than of the gene, that chromosomal
  location is not fixity, and that plasmid fraction and chromosomal
  mobile-element association are largely orthogonal dimensions. No transfer,
  conjugation or horizontal-gene-transfer event is observed or claimed, and this
  repository contains no trained model and no performance claim.
type: software
